## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Canvas A2UI users could make the CLI or agent tool buffer an arbitrarily large JSONL file before validation.

## Why This Change Was Made

Canvas now reads JSONL files through one extension-owned bounded reader for both `--jsonl` and `jsonlPath`. The raw-file ceiling matches the Gateway's 25 MiB frame ceiling: larger source files cannot fit after RPC serialization, while files in the previously valid 8–25 MiB range are no longer rejected by an arbitrary lower product limit.

## User Impact

Oversized A2UI files fail before unbounded buffering, while valid files above the former 8 MiB limit continue through normal validation and node invocation.

## Evidence

- Compatibility case: the prior PR head rejected files above 8 MiB; a 9,437,302-byte valid A2UI payload now passes file reading and validation, then reaches the Gateway connection boundary.
- Oversized negative control: a 26,214,401-byte file is rejected before Gateway connection or unbounded buffering.
- `pnpm exec vitest run extensions/canvas/src/a2ui-jsonl-file.test.ts extensions/canvas/src/cli.test.ts extensions/canvas/src/tool.test.ts`: 38 tests passed.

```text
$ pnpm openclaw nodes canvas a2ui push --node proof-node --jsonl <proof-root>/valid-large.jsonl --url ws://127.0.0.1:1 --token [redacted]
fixture: validBytes=9437302
result: gateway closed ... Gateway target: ws://127.0.0.1:1

$ pnpm openclaw nodes canvas a2ui push --node proof-node --jsonl <proof-root>/oversized.jsonl --url ws://127.0.0.1:1 --token [redacted]
fixture: oversizedBytes=26214401
result: A2UI JSONL file exceeds 26214400 bytes: <proof-root>/oversized.jsonl
```

<details>
<summary>proof-live.ts</summary>

```ts
import { mkdir, open, rm, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import path from "node:path";

const root = path.resolve(process.argv[2] ?? ".tmp/canvas-a2ui-proof");
const gatewayMaxPayloadBytes = 25 * 1024 * 1024;

async function main() {
  await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true });
  await mkdir(root, { recursive: true });
  await writeFile(
    path.join(root, "openclaw.json"),
    JSON.stringify({ plugins: { entries: { canvas: { enabled: true } } } }),
  );

  const valid = JSON.stringify({
    surfaceUpdate: {
      surfaceId: "main",
      components: [
        {
          id: "text",
          component: {
            Text: {
              text: { literalString: "x".repeat(9 * 1024 * 1024) },
            },
          },
        },
      ],
    },
  });
  await writeFile(path.join(root, "valid-large.jsonl"), valid);

  const oversizedPath = path.join(root, "oversized.jsonl");
  const oversized = await open(oversizedPath, "w");
  await oversized.truncate(gatewayMaxPayloadBytes + 1);
  await oversized.close();

  console.log(`validBytes=${Buffer.byteLength(valid)}`);
  console.log(`oversizedBytes=${gatewayMaxPayloadBytes + 1}`);
  console.log(`root=${root}`);
}

void main().catch((error: unknown) => {
  console.error(error);
  process.exitCode = 1;
});
```

</details>

